8. ATTENDANCE MANAGEMENT
====================================================

Implement real server-side attendance.

Employees can:
- Check in.
- Check out.
- View today's attendance.
- View daily and monthly history.
- See late, present, half-day, and missing-checkout statuses.

Rules:
- Timestamps must be generated and validated on the server.
- Reject duplicate check-in with HTTP 409.
- Reject invalid check-out.
- Mark arrivals after 09:15 as Late.
- If recorded working time is below 5 hours, classify it as Half-day according to the defined calculation.
- Identify missing checkout explicitly.
- If no attendance record exists and there is no approved leave on a working day, classify the employee as Absent.
- Exclude configured weekends and company holidays from ordinary absence calculations.
- Consider approved leave when determining absence.

HR/Admin:
- Attendance calendar and reports.
- Employee, department, date, and status filters.
- Corrections with a mandatory reason.
- Audit history containing original value, corrected value, actor, timestamp, and reason.

Do not trust timestamps submitted by the browser. Optional camera/geolocation checks must not block core attendance.

